    challenging: "One of you wants a loyal, settled partner; the other wants a bigger life and keeps adding to it. More travel, more friends, more plans, and less time at home. Commitment feels like it's competing with opportunity. You two fight about excess: money spent, promises made to other people. The upside: nobody feels trapped. The trap is growth that leaves one partner behind. The move: before saying yes to anything big, ask 'does this fit us?'",
